+   /*
+    * RK3576 depthwise weight layout.
+    *
+    * Established on hardware by capturing the vendor runtime weight buffer for
+    * a depthwise layer whose kernel encodes its own (channel, ky, kx) position,
+    * then reading back which byte tracks which weight.  The CMAC consumes the
+    * depthwise weights in a different format than the RK3588 contiguous packing
+    * below; feeding it the RK3588 layout leaves the depthwise CORE unit unable
+    * to start (it never opens, the job hangs).
+    *
+    * The buffer is KH*KW spatial blocks in row-major (ky outer, kx inner)
+    * order.  Each block packs the channels two at a time, every channel pair
+    * followed by the two channels' weight zero points, i.e. two bytes per
+    * channel:
+    *
+    *   buf[p*block + g*4 + 0] = w[2g  ][ky][kx]   (p = ky*KW + kx)
+    *   buf[p*block + g*4 + 1] = w[2g+1][ky][kx]
