+   /*
+    * RK3576 first-conv (ARGB) weight layout.
+    *
+    * Established on hardware by capturing the board's working weight buffer for
+    * a first-conv whose kernel encodes its own (oc, ic, ky, kx) position, then
+    * reading back which byte tracks which weight. Unlike the generic RK3588
+    * packing below, the CNA reads a compact 1536-byte buffer (= 0x101c weight
+    * DMA byte count) for this 3-in/32-out 3x3 layer; feeding it the RK3588
+    * layout makes the CMAC convolve garbage weights (conv0 output = zero-point).
+    *
+    * Layout is ky-MAJOR, then oc, then kx, then ic:
+    *
+    *   buf[ky*(OC*16) + oc*16 + kx*4 + ic] = w[oc][ky][kx][ic] - 0x80   (ic 0..2)
+    *   buf[... + kx*4 + 3]                 = pad (weight_zp - 0x80)       (alpha lane)
+    *   the 4th kx slot (kx=3, bytes 12..15 of each oc unit)             = 0
+    *
+    * So each (ky, oc) is a 16-byte unit of three [R,G,B,pad] groups plus a zero
+    * group; ky stride = OC*16 = 512, oc stride = 16. Total = KH * OC * 16 = 1536.
+    */
