+ * single PC job (task_number = total tasks, one OP_EN) the way the vendor does.
+ *
+ * The PC sequencer, given PC_DATA_ADDR = first task's regcmd and task_number = N,
+ * runs N tasks back-to-back by striding a fixed (pc_data_amount+1)*scale u64 each
+ * time; pc_data_amount is derived (in the kernel) from task[0]'s regcmd_count. So
+ * every task must occupy the SAME stride. We size the stride from the largest task
+ * and zero-pad the rest (the PC reads padding entries as NOPs: tgt=0/reg=0/val=0).
